Below are the columns that matter for the requested analysis and the conditions that will most likely be used.

Relevant columns and their potential usage
• sample_info.Super_Population : label each individual as a case (EAS) or a control (¬ EAS).  
• sample_info.Sample       : primary key to join with call.call_set_name.  
• variants.reference_name   : restrict rows to chromosome 12 (‘12’).  
• variants.start , variants.end : genomic co‑ordinates to be returned.  
• variants.alternate_bases    : restrict to biallelic sites (ARRAY_LENGTH = 1).  
• variants.call                  : array that stores one STRUCT per sample containing the genotype array.  
    – call.call_set_name    : join field to sample name.  
    – call.genotype       : two integers (0 = ref, 1 = alt, -1 = missing).  
• Any computed counts must satisfy the condition that the EXPECTED allele counts in the 2 × 2 table are ≥ 5.

Typical filter / join conditions
reference_name = '12'  
ARRAY_LENGTH(alternate_bases) = 1                    -- biallelic sites only  
gt IN (0,1)                                          -- ignore missing (‑1)  
Super_Population = 'EAS'        → cases  
Super_Population <> 'EAS'       → controls  

